            <ArticleTitle>Foreign Body Stocked between Vocal Cords.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-248</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Foreign body (FB) aspiration is a rare event in adults and can mimic other pathologies such as refractory asthma. Most of the objects can be removed using a bronchoscope. Herein, we present a unique case of aspiration of a FB stocked between vocal cords for one week and the anesthetic considerations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
